### 3. Rewrite `src/cli/init/renderWarning/index.ts` so each deferred category carries its own follow-up surface

Read:
- `coding-playbook/foundations/conventions` — JSDoc, naming, no commented-out content
- `coding-playbook/agentic/agentic` — agent-readable code; user-facing CLI text is part of the agent surface when the cli is invoked from agent loops

The current renderer assumes all deferred categories share a single
follow-up command (`/aide:init`), surfaced via the closing "Next step"
line at line 70. The spec's per-category mapping breaks that assumption —
vault path, brain scaffolding, and IDE each route to a different surface.
The right shape is to drop the "Next step" line and let each category
entry carry its own follow-up inline (the wording is supplied by the
orchestrator in step 1).

- [x] 3a. Edit the deferred-categories heading at line 62. Current:
  `"  Deferred categories (require /aide:init in Claude Code):"`.
  New text must (a) not name a single follow-up command, (b) make clear
  that each entry below names its own follow-up. Suggested phrasing:
  `"  Deferred (each item names how to finish it):"`. The implementor
  may rephrase as long as the parenthetical does not name `/aide:init`
  and the heading reads as a list-introducer, not a command directive.

- [x] 3b. Delete the closing "Next step:" / "Open Claude Code in this
  project and run /aide:init to finish setup." pair (lines 69–70) and
  the blank line above them (line 68). The closing border (line 72) and
  the blank line before it (line 71) are preserved — the block still
  ends with a heavy `=` border. Visually the warning becomes:

  ```
  ============================================================
    SETUP INCOMPLETE — ACTION REQUIRED
  ============================================================

    Skipped files (already on disk or write failed — not overwritten):
      1. <path> — <message>
      ...

    Deferred (each item names how to finish it):
      1. Vault path — open Claude Code and run /aide; the orchestrator will prompt for the path
      2. Brain vault scaffolding — follows the vault path above (same /aide run)
      3. IDE configuration — re-run npx aidemd-mcp init --ide <choice>

  ============================================================
  ```

  The exact category strings come from the orchestrator (step 1); the
  renderer just numbers them. The closing border stays because it
  bookends the block and matches the heading's visual weight.

- [x] 3c. Update the JSDoc block at lines 5–31 to reflect the new
  shape. Specifically: (a) the suppression rule (line 12) is unchanged —
  same condition (`skipped + failed + deferred === 0`); (b) the
  skipped-files subsection rules (lines 18–22) are unchanged; (c) the
  deferred-categories subsection rule (lines 24–25) is unchanged in
  trigger but now ALSO documents that each entry contains its own
  follow-up surface, and that the renderer no longer prints a single
  "Next step" footer; (d) the heavy-borders paragraph (lines 27–30) is
  unchanged.

- [x] 3d. Verify `src/cli/init/renderWarning/index.ts` contains zero
  occurrences of the literal `/aide:init`. Two occurrences must drop
  to zero.

